      "content": "Pause immediately and sit or lie down flat to prevent falling while the dizziness subsides, as sudden head trauma can sometimes cause temporary blood flow changes that mimic concussion symptoms. While waiting for instructions from a doctor, avoid screens, heavy lifting, or standing for long periods until you feel completely stable, and focus on breathing deeply to help your ears and brain recover. Given the fall and new symptoms like dizziness and light sensitivity, you should contact your doctor or seek medical evaluation before returning to work, as relying on \"natural\" fixes for potential head injuries is unsafe. Please prioritize your health over work right now.",
